0..77 Comment "//! A category with families as a theory whose sorts depend on earlier sorts."
78..158 Comment "//! Contexts and substitutions form a category, a type lives in a context, and a"
159..191 Comment "//! term has a type in a context"
192..268 Comment "//! [Huang-2026-fat_cell_structures_generalized_algebraic_theories], § 1.1."
269..272 Comment "//!"
273..344 Comment "//! Dependent type theory states its syntax and its models through this"
345..418 Comment "//! signature. `Tm(g, a)` reads `a` at the sort `Ty(g)`, so a term\'s sort"
419..496 Comment "//! names the context of its type. Comprehension extends a context by a type,"
497..575 Comment "//! and substitution moves types and terms between contexts. The block\'s value"
576..645 Comment "//! of `Theory` keeps each index as data, so a program reads it back."
646..649 Comment "//!"
650..724 Comment "//! The standard model reads a context as a type. A type in a context is a"
725..801 Comment "//! family over it, and a term is a section of that family. The block states"
802..877 Comment "//! the category laws and the laws on types. Their rules carry each context"
878..950 Comment "//! that a substitution stands between, so two identities compose at one"
951..1020 Comment "//! context and the unit laws join. The twin keeps the laws on terms."
1021..1024 Comment "//!"
1025..1040 Comment "//! - see: #522"
1041..1057 Comment "//! - see: #5016"
1058..1074 Comment "//! - see: #5017"
1075..1091 Comment "//! - see: #5042"
1092..1168 Comment "//! - cites: [Huang-2026-fat_cell_structures_generalized_algebraic_theories]"
